Rāvaṇa heeds Vibhīṣaṇa and spares messenger death for tail burning --- Rākṣasas wrap tail with cotton cloths oil and fire --- Hanumān grows like fire and endures to survey Laṅkā --- Rākṣasas parade bound Hanumān through city squares --- Rākṣasīs tell Sītā of burning-tailed monkey parade --- Sītā prays Agni be cool if she is faithful --- Fire burns mild and spares Hanumān tail --- Hanumān recalls Rāma power and Sītā grace --- Hanumān shrinks breaks bonds and seizes tōraṇa beam --- Hanumān slays guards and blazes like sun
